Apple today added two new Golden Gate-themed wallpaper options in the sixth beta of macOS 27.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/08/macos-golden-gate-day-wallpaper.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1059901" /><br/>
There are new Golden Gate Day and Golden Gate Evening wallpaper options that join the Golden Gate Sunset and Golden Gate Night wallpapers that Apple introduced in earlier betas.<br/>
<br/>
macOS 27 also includes abstract Golden Gate wallpaper options for those who don't prefer scenery.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/08/macos-golden-gate-night-wallpaper.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1059902" /><br/>
Golden Gate Day and Golden Gate Evening animate when you unlock your Mac, and can be set as a screen saver. When used as screen saver, both wallpapers feature cars slowly driving across the bridge.<br/>
<br/>
Apple also tweaked the look of the traffic light buttons in <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macos-27/">macOS Golden Gate</a> beta six, adding a Liquid Glass aesthetic. <br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/08/macos-golden-gate-liquid-glass.jpg" alt="" width="236" height="133" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1059903" /><br/>
